First, let's check what happens to the base when x approaches 0. Remember that sin θ ≈ θ - θ³/6 + ... for small θ, so sin 2x ≈ 2x - (2x)³/6 + ... = 2x - 8x³/6 + ... So sin 2x / x ≈ (2x - 8x³/6)/x = 2 - 4x²/3 + ... So as x approaches 0, sin 2x / x approaches 2. So the base approaches 2, which is a positive number not equal to 1. The exponent is 1 + x, which approaches 1 as x approaches 0. So if both the
